        "facts": ["Cuneiform developed in Mesopotamia around 3200 BCE.", "Writing was invented independently more than once.", "Many languages have been spoken without being written."],
        "misconceptions": ["Writing is the same thing as language.", "All writing systems descend from one original invention."] },
      { "key": "types", "title": "Classify writing systems by type", "description": "Distinguishes logographic, syllabic, alphabetic, abjad and abugida systems with examples.",
